{
  "_comment": [
    "Japanese sound effects pinned to an English rendering, applied after the",
    "LLM so an effect cannot come back as romaji or drift between pages. Applied",
    "only to text the detector labels as onomatopoeia.",
    "",
    "The model usually letters a sound effect in English, but sometimes returns",
    "romaji instead -- the same source can come back as 'Eek!' once and 'Kya!'",
    "once. These entries pin the English where it is not in doubt.",
    "",
    "origin:  measured  -- the model's own English, pinned so it cannot regress.",
    "         corrected -- replaces a romaji rendering.",
    "",
    "Effects whose English would be a guess are deliberately absent: a wrong pin",
    "is permanent, a wrong generation is not. Punctuation, symbols and OCR noise",
    "are absent too."
  ],
  "_schema": {
    "source": "the Japanese as OCR returns it",
    "target": "the English to letter",
    "origin": "measured | corrected"
  },
